    <!-- HELP Screen -->

    <string name="help">Help</string>
    <string name="help_folder">Folder :</string>
    <string name="help_folder_text">"A long click on a folder opens the 'modify folder' page."
    "Then you will be able to rename / delete / reset progress</string>
    <string name="help_file">Track :</string>
    <string name="help_file_text">"A long click on a track opens the 'modify track' page."
    "Then you will be able to rename / change order / delete / reset progress</string>
    <string name="help_import">Import :</string>
    <string name="help_import_text">"Zip file are always a bit slower, to import, to load, to play"</string>
    <string name="help_import_text2">"If you have trouble importing your audio :
        \nZIP : In filepicker, if a click on a zip shows the content of the zip instead of letting you select the zip , try a long click on the zip.
        \nZIP : If Unzip fails, try tp unzip them before with another app.
        \nIf problem with picking audios from Download folder, try to move them out of 'Download' folder."</string>
    <string name="help_head_10">Permissions :</string>
    <string name="help_text_10">"BookPlayer will need only a few permission : Notably the right to read phone storage/memory, in order to retrieve and play audio files"</string>
    <string name="help_head_20">Options :</string>
    <string name="help_text_20">"1*/ AutoSleep/AutomaticPause  => BookPlayer will stop playing after XX minutes of inactivities. (useful if you fall asleep)
        \n2*/ Automatic source file deletion => When you import a Zip file in Bookplayer, for example from your phone Download folder, Bookplayer will then, upon successful integration, delete this file
        \n3*/ Freeze Bookplayer Orientation in Portrait Mode while playing audios.
        \n4*/ Custom duration for >> and &lt;&lt; buttons."
    </string>
    <string name="help_head_30">Memory Cleaning :</string>
    <string name="help_text_30">"A specific view to check the content of the Bookplayer internal memory does now exist. It allows to see which book take a lot of room. You can delete some of them from here.
        \nPlease note that, only books that you have loaded through a zip file, are copied inside this reserved Bookplayer memory section. Other books (integrated as a single file, or as a folder) are not stored inside the reserved Bookplayer memory. They should still be located where they were originally (that is to say on the general device memory, like the 'Download' directory) providing they haven't been deleted by another app or user."
    </string>


